::  name       flow-source layer
::  shape      a style: layer that sets the derived-node accent (flow) only
::  invariant  the flow token stays warm/low-blue; ground, head, and read are other layers' to set
::  example    a deep honey derived node, composable over any mode or accent layer
::  readers    brush_parse.rye → tokens.resolve → realidream_view_derived_theme
::  nib        surface-wade1-derived-node-v0
::
::  A .brush *accent* layer for Realidream's derived node — the downstream end of the
::  fused edge: it names only the `flow` token — a deep honey that sets a computed
::  program node apart from the read origin it consumes — and leaves the ground
::  (paper/ink), the read origin (read), and the living edge (head) for other layers to
::  set. Infused over tokens.rye's base sheet, it proves the derived node is themeable on
::  its own key, without touching the ink, the edge rule, the read origin, or the
::  living-edge accent. The cascade is per-key infuse (Bron over Bron), never a CSS rail.
::  Tongue: Glow · Bron · TAME · Radiant. Never JS · HTML · CSS · JSON.
::
::  at-nib:     realidream-derived-node
::  present:    Frame
::  max-lines:  8
::  style:
::    flow 0xFFD2882A
::  lines:
::    realidream view, derived-node theme
::  refuse:     src/web · Wasm/Web backend · CSS rail · a { } stylesheet
